---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import TopAppBar from '../../../components/sections/top-app-bar/TopAppBar.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/sections/footer/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy: UX Design Skill | Creative Sparks">
  <TopAppBar />
  <main class="py-20 md:py-28">
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 prose-custom">
      <h1 class="font-headline font-bold text-4xl md:text-5xl text-foreground tracking-tight leading-[1.1] mb-4">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm font-label text-muted mb-12">Last updated: 2026-11-11</p>

      <p class="text-sm bg-surface-primary p-5 border-l-4 border-primary mb-12"><strong>Note:</strong> This is an English translation provided for convenience. The Polish version of this policy is the legally binding version under Polish law. If there is any conflict between this English version and the Polish version, the Polish version controls. See the <a href="/ux-design-skill/polityka-prywatnosci/">Polish privacy policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>Data controller</h2>
      <p>The controller of your personal data is Tomasz Maciąg, running a sole proprietorship under the business name "Creative Sparks Tomasz Maciąg", Na Polance 10B/10, 51-109 Wrocław, Poland. Tax ID (NIP): 7722112640.</p>
      <p>Contact: <a href="mailto:tomasz@creativesparks.pl">tomasz@creativesparks.pl</a></p>

      <h2>What data I collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email address</strong>, provided when you sign up for the waitlist or at purchase.</li>
        <li><strong>Billing details</strong>, if you provide company details at purchase (company name, tax ID, address).</li>
        <li><strong>Technical data</strong>, IP address and browser type, collected automatically by the server.</li>
        <li><strong>Online service data</strong>, the address of the analyzed page and your IP address, which I store for rate limits only as a cryptographic hash.</li>
        <li><strong>Reports sent through the skill</strong>, the title and content of feedback or a bug report, and your email address if you give it.</li>
        <li><strong>Visit statistics</strong>, the pages you visit, the page you came from, browser, operating system, device type, language, approximate location (country, region, city) and selected actions such as a button click or a purchase (without your email address); collected without cookies by my own Umami instance, which does not store your IP address and tells visits apart by a cryptographic hash of your IP address, your browser and a value that changes regularly.</li>
        <li><strong>Session recordings and heatmaps</strong>, how you move through the product pages (such as cursor movements, clicks and scrolling), only if you consent to statistics cookies; PostHog does not store your IP address.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why I collect data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To fulfill your order and deliver the product (GDPR article 6(1)(b), performance of a contract).</li>
        <li>To issue a VAT invoice (GDPR article 6(1)(c), legal obligation).</li>
        <li>To inform you about product updates (GDPR article 6(1)(b), performance of a contract).</li>
        <li>Newsletter / waitlist, based on your consent (GDPR article 6(1)(a)).</li>
        <li>To run the online service and enforce its rate limits (GDPR article 6(1)(b), performance of a contract).</li>
        <li>To publish and handle feedback and bug reports you choose to send through the skill (GDPR article 6(1)(a), consent).</li>
        <li>Statistics and improving the pages: counting visits with Umami, based on my legitimate interest in measuring traffic on the site (GDPR article 6(1)(f)); session recordings and heatmaps with PostHog, based on your consent (GDPR article 6(1)(a)), which you can withdraw at any time in the cookie settings.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who I share data with</h2>
      <p>Your data may be shared only with the entities necessary to provide the service:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Easytools</strong>, checkout, issuing VAT invoices on my behalf, mailing list and skill delivery.</li>
        <li><strong>Stripe</strong>, online payment processing.</li>
        <li><strong>Meta</strong>, ad performance measurement (including a one-way hash of your email address when you sign up), if you consent to marketing cookies.</li>
        <li><strong>PostHog</strong>, session recordings and heatmaps on the product pages (UX Design Skill and the free skills), if you consent to statistics cookies; data is stored in the EU (Frankfurt).</li>
        <li><strong>Vercel</strong>, servers for the online service, the feedback server and visit statistics (Umami).</li>
        <li><strong>Neon</strong>, the database for visit statistics (Umami), stored in the EU (Frankfurt).</li>
        <li><strong>Upstash</strong>, rate-limit counters for the online service (IP address hashes only).</li>
        <li><strong>GitHub</strong>, public posting of reports in GitHub Discussions (without your email address).</li>
        <li><strong>Make.com and Google (Gmail)</strong>, forwarding the email address you gave in a report to me.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>PostHog masks what you type into form fields (such as your email address) in recordings, so it is not saved. I summarize recordings with PostHog's AI features: the recording and the session's events (such as page views and clicks) are then sent to the AI model providers PostHog uses as subprocessors (Anthropic, OpenAI and Google).</p>
      <p>Some of these companies may process data outside the European Economic Area, under the mechanisms GDPR provides (for example the EU-US Data Privacy Framework or standard contractual clauses).</p>
      <p>I do not sell or rent your data to third parties.</p>

      <h2>How long I keep data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Order fulfillment data, for the duration of the contract plus 5 years (tax obligation).</li>
        <li>Mailing list data, until you unsubscribe.</li>
        <li>Technical data (server logs), up to 30 days.</li>
        <li>Session recordings (PostHog), 30 days; heatmap data and other PostHog events, up to 1 year.</li>
        <li>Visit statistics (Umami), up to 2 years.</li>
        <li>Online service rate-limit counters expire automatically.</li>
        <li>Reports published in GitHub Discussions, until deleted; you can ask me to delete your report.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access your data.</li>
        <li>Correct your data.</li>
        <li>Erase your data ("right to be forgotten").</li>
        <li>Restrict processing.</li>
        <li>Data portability.</li>
        <li>Object to processing based on my legitimate interest (such as visit statistics).</li>
        <li>Withdraw consent (for the newsletter, and for statistics and marketing cookies in the cookie settings in the footer).</li>
        <li>Lodge a complaint with the President of the Polish Personal Data Protection Office (UODO). Under GDPR, EU and UK residents may also lodge a complaint with their local supervisory authority.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise your rights, write to <a href="mailto:tomasz@creativesparks.pl">tomasz@creativesparks.pl</a>.</p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>The site uses cookies for technical purposes and, if you consent, for statistics (PostHog) and marketing (Meta Pixel). Visit statistics (Umami) work without cookies.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>I may update this policy. I will announce changes on the site. Changes do not apply to data collected before they take effect.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose-custom h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-headline);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-foreground);
    margin-top: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .prose-custom p {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .prose-custom ul, .prose-custom ol {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    padding-left: 0;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .prose-custom ul li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .prose-custom ul li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.45em;
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    background: url("data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg viewBox='0 0 19 22' fill='none' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%3E%3Cpath d='M14.32 12.84L10.24 17.66L8.75 16.77L12.11 12.67L8.75 8.57L10.24 7.7L14.32 12.53V12.84ZM9.54 12.84L5.49 17.66L4 16.77L7.36 12.67L4 8.57L5.49 7.7L9.54 12.53V12.84Z' fill='%23010DFF'/%3E%3C/svg%3E") no-repeat center;
    background-size: contain;
  }
  .prose-custom a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .prose-custom a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .prose-custom strong {
    color: var(--color-foreground);
  }
</style>
